WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.537
A bar chart is useful for comparing values across categories.

00:00:04.537 --> 00:00:12.787
In the example, we first calculate the average order amount for each region, then plot those regional averages.

00:00:12.787 --> 00:00:18.539
The categories are on one axis, and the summary value is represented by bar height.

00:00:19.188 --> 00:00:22.285
A bar chart is different from a histogram.

00:00:22.285 --> 00:00:28.470
A histogram shows the distribution of one numeric variable across numeric ranges.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.360
A bar chart compares discrete categories.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:42.220
When bar length represents magnitude, the numeric axis should usually begin at zero so the visual difference is not

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:47.110
exaggerated. Keep labels readable and avoid unnecessary decoration.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:54.190
The purpose of the chart is to make the category comparison easier to understand than the table alone.
